{"qid": "76997109", "kind": "freshstack", "language": "python", "title": "Using langchain for text to SQL using custom llm API", "answer": "You can use the `SQLDatabase.from_cnosdb()` method to connect to your Postgres database and then use the `OpenAI` class to query the database and generate SQL queries. You'll need to install the `cnos-connector` package and import the `SQLDatabase` class from `langchain_community.utilities`. Here's an example code snippet to get you started:\n\n```python\nimport psycopg2\nfrom langchain_community.utilities import SQLDatabase\nfrom langchain_openai import OpenAI\n\n# Create connection to Postgres\ndatabase = 'postgres'\nusername = 'postgres'\npassword = 'password'\nserver = 'localhost'\nport = '5432'\n\n# Establish the connection\nconn = psycopg2.connect(\n    dbname=database,\n    user=username,\n    password=password,\n    host=server,\n    port=port\n)\ndb = SQLDatabase.from_uri(\n    f", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["llama_index/llama-index-integrations/tools/llama-index-tools-database/README.md_0_1347", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/providers/cnosdb.mdx_0_3963", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/lantern.ipynb_0_6695", "chroma/go/pkg/sysdb/metastore/db/dbcore/core.go_0_5906"], "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/integrations/providers/cnosdb.mdx_0_3963", "llama_index/llama-index-integrations/tools/llama-index-tools-database/README.md_0_1347"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [["langchain/docs/docs/integrations/sql-database/README.md_0_1347", "llama_index/llama-index-integrations/tools/llama-index-tools-database/README.md_0_1347"]], "degenerate_answer": false, "context_coverage": 0.0, "context_recall": 0.0, "nuggets": ["Load the Llama2 model using the method described in the Langchain documentation for Ollama integrations.", "Replace the OpenAI component in the existing code with the Llama2 model.", "Adjust the prompts to fit the Llama2 model's desire